# `schema`

Optional `protocol_constants` points to a checked YAML catalog loaded by `LoadProtocolConstants`. Set/member names must be canonical snake_case; generated names and authored values must be unique within each set. Values are compile-time integration metadata only: they do not alter protobuf tags or the snapshot schema fingerprint.

Event payload fields retain legacy alphabetical numbering when untagged. If any field in an event uses `{ tag: N, type: T }`, every field in that event must use a unique legal direct protobuf tag; entity-targeted events reserve tag 1 for `entity_id`.

**Config, entity, command, and world data definitions:** reads `golem.yaml` (`LoadConfig`), per-entity `.yaml` under the configured `entity_schema` dir (`LoadSchemas`), per-command `.yaml` under the configured `command_schema` dir (`LoadCommands`), and per-world-type `.yaml` under the configured world dir (`LoadWorldSchemas`). Builds `EntityData`, `VarInfo`, `CommandData`, `CommandFieldInfo`, `WorldTypeData`, `WorldFieldInfo`, `WorldUpdateField`, `ProtoTemplateData`, and `SharedData` for generators. Holds **naming helpers** (`ToSnakeCase`, etc.) and **type maps** (proto → Go/TS). Entity var names reserved for metadata (`pos_x`/`pos_y`/`pos_z`/`revision`) and names whose `SnakeToPascal` form is `Server` or `BindServer` (e.g. `server`, `bind_server`, literal `Server`/`BindServer`) are rejected in `BuildEntityData`. Optional entity var `visibility` (`empty`/`all` = public, `owner` = owner-only replication; any other value is a bake error) sets `VarInfo.OwnerOnly`; `EntityData.HasOwnerVars` is true when any var is owner-only. Visibility does not change proto tags or the schema fingerprint. Optional entity `collider` resolves to bake-time `ColliderData` (2D: exactly one of `aabb`/`circle`; 3D: exactly one of `aabb3d`/`sphere`; non-empty `layer`; optional `trigger` default false; positive finite sizes; reject cross-dimension shapes). Optional top-level `collision` (`layers` ≤ 32, symmetric `collides` pairs) resolves via `ResolveCollisionConfig` into `Config.ResolvedCollision` (`yaml:"-"`) at `LoadConfig` and is threaded to `SharedData.Collision` — validate unique non-empty layer names, matrix references, retain self-pairs (e.g. Player/Player), reject duplicate unordered pairs (`[A,B]` and `[B,A]`); collider without `collision:` is a bake error; `collision:` without entity colliders is allowed. Collider/collision metadata is not wire/fingerprint state. Does **not** embed templates, write generated files, or register integrations—that is `codegen/`. Depends only on stdlib + YAML.
